hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"413","Harun ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, Abu Bakr — meaning Ibn 'Ayyash — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sahl, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a woman dies among men with no woman besides her, and a man among women with no man besides him, they are both given tayammum and buried, and they are in the position of one who finds no water."
"414","Hannad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: 'Ali sought from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what is sought from the dead, but did not find it. So he said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, you were pleasant in life and in death."
